Login page: the card sits in the middle of the viewport, not near the top

Footstrap places the login card 7vh below the top of the page (`margin: 7vh auto`),
so on a desktop screen the form hangs in the upper third with empty space under it.
<body> is already a full-height flex column (styles/base: `html { height: 100% }`,
`body { min-height: 100%; display: flex; flex-direction: column }`) and the form is
its direct child, so `margin: auto` centres the card on both axes. When the viewport
is shorter than the card the auto margins resolve to 0 and the page scrolls from the
top as before, so nothing is cut off. A block padding on the login page's <body>
keeps a gap above and below the card on short screens.

Applies to: https://github.com/VizzleTF/luci-theme-footstrap.git
            @ a1711eda02fefe87a12590bae9eaa80c373a4bd9 (pinned in configs/local-packages.pin)
Applied by: tools/cw-release-build.sh, on the pinned commit before the package is
            installed, with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` - the build fails if upstream
            changes these lines; re-port it then.
Upstream status: not submitted (CleanWRT-specific layout).

--- a/luci-theme-footstrap/styles/pages/10-login.css
+++ b/luci-theme-footstrap/styles/pages/10-login.css
@@ -8,11 +8,16 @@
 		/* DEFINITE width, never max-width: a direct flex item of <body> collapses to min-content
 		 * (~131px) under max-width alone — docs/css.md above. */
 		width: min(400px, calc(100% - 32px));
-		margin: 7vh auto var(--fs-space-10);
+		/* auto on every side: <body> is a full-height flex column, so the card sits in the middle
+		 * of the viewport; on a screen shorter than the card the auto margins resolve to 0 and the
+		 * page scrolls from the top. */
+		margin: auto;
 		background: var(--fs-panel); border: var(--fs-hairline); border-radius: var(--fs-radius-lg);
 		/* the token, not a literal 45%-black 60px halo: that ignored the palette. */
 		padding: var(--fs-space-6); box-shadow: var(--fs-shadow-pop);
 	}
+	/* breathing room above and below the centred card when the viewport is barely taller than it */
+	body:has(> .fs-login) { padding-block: var(--fs-space-6); }
